# Cache policy for the static osu!web bundle.
#
# The _framework/ directory and the root *.js modules are content-hashed by the .NET SDK
# (dotnet.<hash>.js, main.<hash>.js, ...), and shell.css is fingerprinted the same way by
# web/make-static-export.ps1 (shell.<hash>.css), so a given URL always refers to the same
# bytes and is safe to cache forever. Without this the browser re-downloads ~130 MB of
# WebAssembly on every page reload.
#
# Everything else uses `no-cache`, which still permits caching -- the browser merely has to
# revalidate first. Static hosts answer that with a cheap 304 Not Modified rather than
# re-sending the body, so reloading stays fast while a re-uploaded build is still picked up
# immediately.
#
# GitHub Pages ignores this file and applies its own 10-minute default instead. That default
# is exactly why the stylesheet is fingerprinted: an unhashed shell.css can be served from
# that cache against a freshly deployed index.html for up to ten minutes, which shows up as
# the previous deploy's styling applied to the new markup.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/_framework/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable